{#- Services (REQ-010): three article.card.service
    blocks on the balanced subgrid — picture band | number | title | text |
    "What you get" heading | list (2–4 items) | action — the seven tracks
    base.css spans. The band is the card's drawing, card-art/<key>.svg
    (si-jwwd), decorative and hidden from assistive technology.
    Headings, texts and lists come from strings.themes.<key> (the keys are
    ai-apps / ai-adoption / experiments — THEME_KEYS in scripts/lib/apps.mjs —
    so the apps data keeps validating; experiments replaced investing in
    founder feedback round 1, si-yp2x); the AI-powered apps card acts through
    the #apps anchor, the AI adoption card through nivå's public page
    (site.nivaUrl, since si-gyc4 — #apps while it is null) and the
    experiments card through the blog index of the page's language. An action
    that leaves the site wears ↗ instead of →, like the app cards' links. The
    copy bands (title ≤ 20 characters, texts within a 45 % band) are asserted
    by tests/apps.test.mjs. -#}
{%- set services = strings[lang].services -%}
{%- set actions = { "ai-apps": "#apps", "ai-adoption": site.nivaUrl or "#apps", "experiments": langPrefix + "/blog/" } -%}
<section id="services" class="section" aria-labelledby="services-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ services.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 id="services-title">{{ services.heading }}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="service-grid">
      {%- for key in ["ai-apps", "ai-adoption", "experiments"] %}
      {%- set theme = strings[lang].themes[key] %}
      <article class="card service reveal">
        <div class="card-band" aria-hidden="true">{% include "card-art/" + key + ".svg" %}</div>
        <p class="num">0{{ loop.index }}</p>
        <h3>{{ theme.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ theme.text }}</p>
        <h4 class="gets-heading">{{ theme.getsHeading }}</h4>
        <ul class="gets">
          {%- for itemKey, item in theme.gets %}
          <li>{{ item }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="{{ actions[key] }}">{{ theme.cta }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">{{ "↗" if actions[key].startsWith("https://") else "→" }}</span></a>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
